Usage: ps [options]

Report a snapshot of the current processes.
Shows information about running processes on Windows.

OPTIONS:
  -e                select all processes (same as -A)
  -A                select all processes
  -a                select all processes except session leaders and not
                    associated with a terminal
  -f                do full-format listing
  -l                long format
  -u                display user-oriented format
  -p, --pid ARG     select processes by process ID
  -o, --format ARG  select output fields
      --user ARG    filter processes by user name
  -x                lift the BSD-style "must have a tty" restriction
  -w                wide output (do not truncate command lines)
      --no-headers  print no header line
      --sort ARG    sort by column (e.g., +pid, -rss)
      --help        display this help and exit
  -V, --version     output version information and exit

EXIT STATUS:
  0  if OK,
  1  if minor problems,
  2  if serious trouble.

WinuxCmd is a Windows implementation of GNU CoreUtils for Linux-Windows developers and AI coding assistants.
